# Enterprise engineering charter (enforcement)

Thin gate only. Full text: `docs/ENGINEERING_CHARTER.md`. Not a second
constitution — product/architecture authority stays in `docs/GOVERNANCE.md`,
Freeze, and ADRs.

## Mandatory before any task

Applies in **Agent, Ask, Plan, review, and docs** work in this repo:

1. Read `docs/ENGINEERING_CHARTER.md` and follow it.
2. For implementation: also read `docs/GOVERNANCE.md` pre-work gate and
   `CONTINUE.md`; inspect current code — never rely on chat memory alone.
3. For Find / Recall / ranking / Why: read `docs/RECALL_ENFORCEMENT_INDEX.md` and
   obey `unfynd-architecture-invariants.mdc` (ARCHITECTURAL BOUNDARY block when
   touching search).

## Pre-flight (state before coding or recommending)

- How does this change affect the rest of the system?
- **Holistic scenarios** (charter): user journeys + technical failure modes +
  explicit acceptance bar **before** implement — not only what an ADR already
  lists. Innovate for user value within architecture; do not ship commodity
  “top-N vectors” without a trust/NL bar when the surface is product Find.
- Edge cases: loading, empty, error, permission, offline, concurrency.
- Security and privacy impact.
- Alternatives considered for non-obvious decisions (include one higher-value
  option vs plain industry default when relevant).
- Smallest safe change; no unnecessary abstractions or dependencies.

## Implementation bar

Production-quality, not prototypes. Handle real failure modes. UX and
accessibility matter. No hacks that only pass the immediate test. Call out flawed
patterns instead of copying them. Surface ambiguity — do not assume.

## Done means

Self-review: bugs, regressions, missing states, weak abstractions, poor UX.
Verify with tests or an explicit documented gate. Work must be understandable to
another senior engineer.

Do not optimize for quick fixes or speed. Optimize for building the right thing
properly.

## Precedence

Explicit **user instruction** in the current message overrides workspace defaults
(e.g. when to git commit). Charter overrides generic assistant habits. Product
docs and Freeze override convenience.
